    report=f"""# NHL season 2026 SOG prospective observation and immutable-capture readiness\n\n## Decision\n\nThe preserved scoring target is `poisson_baseline / baseline_v1` (`NHL_SOG_BASELINE_V1_SEASON_2025`), not the selectable ordinal, calibration, or defense-shadow paths. The historical 40,167-row, 13,389-player-game population achieved Level 4 exact reproduction at lines 1.5, 2.5, and 3.5: probabilities within `1e-12` and zero side mismatches. The current scorer hash is `{scorer_hash}`, but a frozen feature-manifest hash and run-bound wrapper remain prerequisites.\n\nPrediction inputs can be produced, but current feature, prediction, site, and date-archive outputs are mutable and lack run identity. Preserve every rate/TOI fallback input, the chosen sources and values, defaults, expected SOG, identities, start/run times, and available source timestamps. Role, pairing, PP, lineup, goalie, injury, and scratch context stays observational; `NO_SOURCE_READY` goalie context does not block the baseline.\n\n## Workflow finding\n\nThe daily CLI loads schedule and rosters, mutates/fills pregame tables, exports a dated feature CSV, chooses a scorer by environment, overwrites the processed prediction CSV, optionally applies other paths, loads database predictions, fetches current odds, overwrites site market files, and copies fixed filenames into a date directory. Code existence and LaunchAgent/manual remnants are not evidence of an authorized active season-2026 workflow. No unattended schedule is enabled here.\n\nThe odds normalizer recursively extracts outcomes, aliases player names, and aggregates prices by median. Its published SOG CSV omits sportsbook, provider event/market IDs, provider/source timestamp, capture timestamp, raw payload hash, and market status. Same-date archive copies can overwrite. Therefore market and price-time evidence are not ready.\n\nCandidate policy is also blocked: live and historical selectors accept distinct JSON/CLI thresholds and optional caps, shrink, confirmations, exclusions, while upload exporters add filters or bypass candidate identity. No single policy/version/hash is attached rule-by-rule to rows. Uploads omit run, prediction, quote, policy, and export identities and cannot imply execution.\n\n## Prospective contract\n\nRuns use `canonical_season + slate_date + run_timestamp_utc + run_type`, with only `MIDDAY` and `FINAL_PREGAME`, and are create-only. Populations P, C, M, U, E, and G remain distinct. Grading binds certified official SOG and participation to the exact pregame identity in a separate append-only artifact; nonparticipants are never automatic unders. Game types are 1 preseason, 2 regular season, 3 postseason; preseason is `PRESEASON_NON_EVALUATION`, unknown types fail closed, and preseason cannot enter regular-season histories.\n\nHealth gates cover identity, governed model hashes and finite semantics, strict-prior timing, exact quote binding and pregame time, policy rule lineage, and create-only manifests. These are specified, not yet operationally enforced.\n\n## MVP and boundary\n\nMVP requires governed scoring/parity, immutable input and run capture, timestamped raw quotes, one frozen existing candidate policy, population separation, append-only grading, health gates, and manifests. Optional context integrations must not delay it. SOG may share generic identity, time, hash, game-type, and HTTP primitives with mainlines, but never player/market/model/policy/outcome data or run populations.\n\n## Readiness values\n\n```json\n{json.dumps(decisions, indent=2, sort_keys=True)}\n```\n\nExactly one next bounded task is `{next_task}`. It unlocks immutable run-bound quote evidence; it does not unlock candidate activation, full shadow observation, wagering, ROI, retraining, challengers, promotion, automation, or frontend changes.\n"""
